From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Author: Jeremiah Jordan
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:39:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Hints: encrypted under
 transparent_data_encryption_options, fail closed, key outages are not
 corruption

cassandra.yaml documents hints as covered by transparent data encryption, but HintsService never
asked for it; it now does when encryption is enabled and hints are not compressed. A new hints
file whose key cannot be had throws EncryptionKeyUnavailableException instead of being written
unencrypted. A file being read builds its decryptor when it is read, not when the catalog lists
it; when its key cannot be had then, dispatch keeps the file for the next attempt instead of
treating it as corrupt and deleting it. Before each flush, the open hints file asks for its key
again; one whose key may no longer encrypt is closed (it stays readable while its key may
decrypt) and the hints go to a new file under the current key.
---
